{#
   Hero (#top). Centred single column per the redesign — the old hero was a
   two-column split with the Chairman's Terminal in the right-hand column; that
   widget is now its own full-bleed #telemetry section directly below.

   Release status is stated once, here, and the design fixes the wording: live on
   Google Play, iOS via TestFlight. Both CTAs carry data-store-link rather than
   ids, so landing.js wires every store button on the page from one pass instead
   of naming five element ids (there are six store CTAs now: two here, two in
   #testers, two in the closing CTA).

   Every store CTA ships hidden and is revealed by that same pass once it knows
   which platforms have a URL — the buttons are never rendered pointing at "#".
   data-store-link="pending" is the one shown when NEITHER platform resolves, so
   the row is never empty, and #testers carries the fallbacks that work without
   a store URL (see landing.js's five roles).

   #get is on the button row, not the section, because the header's PLAY NOW
   targets it and the design anchors it there.
#}
<section class="hero" id="top">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-inner">
            <p class="hero-kicker vt">MOBILE FOOTBALL CLUB OWNERSHIP SIM</p>

            <h1 class="hero-title">DON'T MANAGE THE CLUB. <span class="glow-gold">OWN IT.</span></h1>

            <p class="hero-sub">
                Hire a Director of Football, build the stadium, grow the fanbase and watch
                your club rise through the divisions. Deep simulation, pixel-art charm and
                no pay-to-win. It plays offline and syncs weekly across
                {{ world.totals.tierCount }} tiers and
                {{ world.totals.leaderboardCategories }} global leaderboards.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-actions" id="get">
                <a href="#" class="btn btn-gold btn-lg" data-store-link="android" style="display:none">GET IT ON GOOGLE PLAY</a>
                <a href="#" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" data-store-link="ios" style="display:none">JOIN ON TESTFLIGHT</a>
                {# Shown only when neither store link resolves, so the row is never
                   empty — including when /api/app-links fails outright. #}
                <a href="#testers" class="btn btn-gold btn-lg" data-store-link="pending" style="display:none">GET THE GAME</a>
            </div>

            <p class="hero-release vt">Live on Google Play. iOS available through TestFlight.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
